<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Themistocles</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 524–459 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Themistocles was an Athenian statesman and general who persuaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> to build a large fleet with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laurion">Laurion</a>. He led the Greek fleet to victory over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a> at Salamis in 480 BCE and had the walls of Athens rebuilt. Later ostracised and accused of treason, he fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artaxerxes-i">Artaxerxes I</a> gave him the revenues of several Anatolian cities.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/themistocles.jpg" alt="Themistocles" width="320" height="559" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Evald Hansen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Illustrerad_Verldshistoria_band_I_Ill_116.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
